---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import EuBadges from '../components/EuBadges.astro';

const sources = (await getCollection('sources')).map(e => e.data);
const dests   = (await getCollection('destinations')).map(e => e.data);
const countBy = (id: string) => dests.filter(d => d.dataSource === id).length;
const connected = sources.filter(s => s.status === 'connected').length;
const booking = (await import('../data/booking-systems.json')).default as any[];
const golf = booking.filter(b => b.vertical === 'golf');
const resto = booking.filter(b => b.vertical === 'restaurant');
---
<Base title="For national and regional tourism organisations" angle="nto" concierge
      description="The ontology layer that makes national tourism data readable by every assistant, agent and search engine.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14">
    <p class="mb-3 text-xs font-bold tracking-widest text-(--color-slate2) uppercase">
      For national &amp; regional tourism organisations
    </p>
    <h1 class="h-display">The ontology layer<br />under your tourism data.</h1>
    <p class="lede mt-5">
      You have invested in a national data platform. The remaining gap is semantic: assistants, agents
      and search engines cannot reason over your records without a shared model of what a <em>trail</em>,
      an <em>opening period</em> or a <em>tasting room</em> actually is. That layer is what we operate —
      across {connected} national and regional platforms today.
    </p>
    <EuBadges />
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-(--color-line-2) bg-(--color-paper-2) py-12">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5">
      <h2 class="h-section">Connected platforms and licence attribution</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-(--color-ink-2)">
        Attribution is rendered wherever the licence requires it — on the destination page and in its
        machine-readable record. Where a connector is only planned, we publish no attribution at all.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[680px] border-collapse text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-(--color-line) text-left text-xs tracking-widest text-(--color-ink-3) uppercase">
              <th class="p-3">Geography</th><th class="p-3">Platform</th>
              <th class="p-3">Connector</th><th class="p-3">Attribution as published</th><th class="p-3">Live</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {sources.map(s => (
              <tr class="border-b border-(--color-line-2)">
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold">{s.geo}
                  {s.coverage && <span class="mt-0.5 block text-xs font-normal text-(--color-ink-3)">{s.coverage}</span>}
                </td>
                <td class="p-3"><a class="font-semibold text-(--color-pine) underline" href={`/data/${s.id}`}>{s.name}</a></td>
                <td class="p-3">
                  <span class={`rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-semibold ${
                    s.status === 'connected' ? 'bg-(--color-pine-l) text-(--color-pine)' : 'bg-(--color-amber-l) text-(--color-amber)'}`}>
                    {s.status === 'connected' ? 'Connected' : 'Planned'}
                  </span>
                </td>
                <td class="p-3 text-xs italic text-(--color-ink-3)">
                  {s.status === 'connected' ? s.attribution : '— not claimed until the connector is live'}
                </td>
                <td class="p-3">{countBy(s.id)}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="h-section">Four things the layer does</h2>
        <dl class="mt-6 space-y-5">
          {[['Normalise','One entity model across every source, so a Finnish record and a Korean record answer the same question the same way.'],
            ['Enrich','Live availability, ratings, classifications and accessibility — plus an owner-supplied overlay that never overwrites your record.'],
            ['Expose','schema.org, JSON-LD, an MCP endpoint and llms.txt, so any assistant can cite your destinations correctly.'],
            ['Govern','Licence terms, attribution and provenance carried through to the answer, per field.']
          ].map(([t,b]) => (
            <div>
              <dt class="font-semibold">{t}</dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-(--color-ink-2)">{b}</dd>
            </div>
          ))}
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="mb-2 text-sm text-(--color-ink-3)">A destination record, as published</p>
        <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-(--color-ink) p-5 text-xs leading-relaxed text-[#C6D2CC]">{`GET /api/destinations/nancy.json

{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "TouristDestination",
  "name": "Nancy",
  "source": {
    "platform": "DATAtourisme",
    "attribution": "DATAtourisme, Licence
                    Ouverte / Etalab",
    "refresh": "continuous"
  },
  "enrichmentLayer": { "affectsRanking": false },
  "agentEndpoint": "mcp://dm2find.ai/nancy"
}`}</pre>
        <p class="mt-3 border-l-4 border-(--color-line) pl-4 text-sm text-(--color-ink-3)">
          Publishing this makes the infrastructure claim demonstrable — and positions your destinations
          to be <em>cited</em> by assistants rather than fighting for blue links.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-(--color-line-2) bg-(--color-paper-2) py-12">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-5 px-5 sm:grid-cols-3">
      {[['Sovereignty','Built in the EU and hosted on our own European infrastructure, with an optional fully-European model stack from source to answer. The one exception is the optional voice agent, which runs on ElevenLabs in the US — it is never part of the data layer, and it only loads when a visitor starts it.'],
        ['Non-exclusive','We sit beside your platform, not in front of it. Your data stays yours; attribution travels with it, per field.'],
        ['Rollout','Pilot three destinations, then extend nationally with per-DMO branding on one shared layer.']
      ].map(([t,b]) => (
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-(--color-line) bg-white p-5">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold">{t}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-(--color-ink-2)">{b}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="booking" class="border-t border-(--color-line-2) bg-(--color-paper-2) py-14">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5">
      <p class="mb-3 text-xs font-bold tracking-widest text-(--color-ink-3) uppercase">Booking systems</p>
      <h2 class="h-section">The ontology reaches past open data.</h2>
      <p class="lede mt-4">
        Open tourism data says a golf course exists. It cannot say whether Saturday at 08:40 is free —
        that lives in the club's own tee sheet and changes by the minute. We read&nbsp;
        <b>16 tee-sheet systems and 29 restaurant reservation platforms</b>, so a venue never changes
        software to work with us.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-(--color-line) bg-white p-6">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold">Golf — 16 systems</h3>
          <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
            {golf.map(b => (
              <span class={`rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold ${
                b.mode === 'api' ? 'bg-(--color-pine-l) text-(--color-pine)'
                                 : 'bg-(--color-paper-3) text-(--color-ink-2)'}`}>{b.name}</span>
            ))}
            <span class="rounded-full bg-white px-3 py-1 text-xs text-(--color-ink-3) ring-1 ring-(--color-line)">
              and 7 more
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-(--color-line) bg-white p-6">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold">Restaurants — 29 systems</h3>
          <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
            {resto.map(b => (
              <span class={`rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold ${
                b.mode === 'api' ? 'bg-(--color-pine-l) text-(--color-pine)'
                                 : 'bg-(--color-paper-3) text-(--color-ink-2)'}`}>{b.name}</span>
            ))}
            <span class="rounded-full bg-white px-3 py-1 text-xs text-(--color-ink-3) ring-1 ring-(--color-line)">
              and 20 more
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-(--color-line) bg-white p-5">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold">Live lookup</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-(--color-ink-2)">
            Green pills read availability directly. The visitor gives a date and a party size inside the
            conversation and gets an answer back.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-(--color-line) bg-white p-5">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold">Direct link</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-(--color-ink-2)">
            Grey pills — Golfmanager and Nexxchange — hand over to the venue's own booking page instead.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-(--color-amber) bg-(--color-amber-l) p-5">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold">We never take the booking</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-(--color-ink-2)">
            No payment, no inventory held, no commission. We show what is free; the venue completes the
            reservation on its own system.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-(--color-line) bg-white p-6">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold">Which system do you use?</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 max-w-[70ch] text-sm text-(--color-ink-2)">
          If it is not listed above, it is probably still one of the 45 we read — and if it genuinely
          is not, tell us which one and we will say plainly whether we can.
        </p>
        <form class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2" action="mailto:sales@dm2find.ai" method="get">
          <input type="hidden" name="subject" value="Booking system" />
          <input name="body" placeholder="e.g. Nappkin, Avenista, teeitup…"
                 class="min-w-[16rem] flex-1 rounded-xl border border-(--color-line) bg-white px-4 py-2.5 text-sm outline-none focus:border-(--color-pine)" />
          <button class="rounded-full bg-(--color-pine) px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white">Ask</button>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
